---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import bobPortrait from '../assets/images/bob-zybach.jpg';

const title = 'About — Oregon Websites & Watersheds Project';
const description = 'About the Oregon Websites & Watersheds Project, Bob Zybach the program manager, and the NW Maps Co. imprint.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} activeNav="about">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl mb-8 font-serif font-semibold text-orww-navy">About</h1>

    <section class="prose-orww max-w-measure">
      <h2>About this project</h2>
      <p>
        The Oregon Websites and Watersheds Project, Inc. is a 501(c)(3) educational nonprofit founded in 1996 by Wayne Giesy (1928–2019) and Bob Zybach. Wayne's original Idea Hour broadcast in Tillamook County in the 1980s; ORWW's first sustained digital project was the PEAS Program (Public Education and Action through Science), launched in 1996. ORWW publishes educational content on Pacific Northwest forestry, watershed resources, fire ecology, native plants, and Oregon historical ecology. The project's Wayne Giesy / Bob Zybach origin story, the PEAS Program lineage, and the dual-imprint structure (ORWW + NW Maps Co.) are all documented in the project's own archive at <a href="http://www.orww.org/">www.orww.org</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 sm:gap-8 items-start">
      <figure class="sm:order-2 w-full sm:w-60 shrink-0 mx-auto sm:mx-0">
        <Image
          src={bobPortrait}
          alt="Bob Zybach, ORWW Program Manager"
          widths={[240, 320, 480]}
          sizes="(min-width: 640px) 240px, 80vw"
          format="webp"
          quality={85}
          class="w-full h-auto border border-orww-rule rounded-sm"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center font-sans italic text-sm text-orww-ink-mute">
          Bob Zybach, Program Manager, ORWW.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="sm:order-1 prose-orww max-w-measure">
        <h2 class="mt-0">About Bob Zybach, Program Manager</h2>
        <p>
          Bob Zybach holds a PhD in Environmental Sciences from Oregon State University (2003), where his dissertation reconstructed the catastrophic-scale fire history of the Oregon Coast Range from 1491 to 1951 — a 500-year baseline of pre-European-settlement and early-historic burns that remains a unique credentialed asset in the field. Bob is a historical ecologist, author of <em>The Elliott: An Anthology</em> (Zybach Forestry Anthologies), and the program manager of ORWW since the organization's founding. His current and recent fieldwork includes the 1828 Umpqua Memorial Project, the Osbornes Project (GPS-paired historical and contemporary panoramic photography), and the ongoing Letitia Carson biography. He has testified before the Oregon Legislature on Elliott State Forest matters and teaches forestry students at Southwestern Oregon Community College using the Elliott as an outdoor classroom. He is available for consulting, expert witness work, speaking engagements, and substantive licensing of ORWW's photographic and documentary archive — contact details below.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 prose-orww max-w-measure">
        <h2>About NW Maps Co.</h2>
      <p>
        NW Maps Co. is Bob Zybach's professional consulting and publishing imprint, founded 1994. It holds the proprietary research, photography, maps, and writings that ORWW publishes in its educational mission. The split between the two organizations is functional: ORWW is the charitable face that hosts publicly accessible material; NW Maps Co. is the for-profit vehicle through which Bob licenses commercial uses of his proprietary work. Both organizations operate from the same office in Cottage Grove, Oregon. Commercial licensing inquiries should be directed to NW Maps Co. via the contact information below.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Bob Zybach, PhD</strong><br />
        ORWW Program Manager / NW Maps Co.<br />
        <span class="text-orww-ink-mute italic">[email pending — Bob to supply]</span><br />
        <span class="text-orww-ink-mute italic">[phone pending — Bob to supply]</span>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6">
        <a href="/contact/">More on contact and the four kinds of inquiries this site might generate →</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
